Z||000000||Standard||01-16-2001||10:50 PM||||Who else wastes way too much time with this game?  I'm pretty much addicted to it.. best racing game I've ever found!  Only problem is it has a tendancy to randomly lock up.. doesn't stop me from playing, tho.  I have a bunch of replays if anyone wants to see my mad skills  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I'd have to say my favorite car is the '88 944 Turbo S Coupe, that thing just rules!  Plus, I've always like 944's, and I want to buy one sometime.. it's also about the only porsche I could afford, too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If anyone wants some help with the game I can send ya my save file.. I'm at 1989 with about $2,000,000 and every car made up to that point  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Everybody wants a normal life and a cool car.. <B>Most people settle for the car</B><P>I'm not dumb.  I just have a command of thoroughly useless information        <BR>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd<BR>AIM: Standard88||||reg||14
Z||000001||Songman||01-17-2001||08:51 AM||||I can't figure out how to get to anywhere on this game other than the test track... When I select my car, all it does it sit there and go around with me opening the doors and trunk! heheh<P>Looks like it would be a fun game though!<P>I downloaded a Fiero someone had for NFS3 the other day. I don't have 3 so I tried it with NFS4. Doesn't work... Guess I'll either have to get NFS3 or find a Fiero for NFS4.||||reg||1
Z||000002||p4n1c||01-17-2001||09:48 AM||||If you've patched NFS4, no modified cars will work with it.  EA took the support out to stop cheating on their internet game forum.<P>NFS:PU just rules.  A friend of mine and I got bored one night, turned off the damage and sat on one track for about an hour seeing how high we could flip the GT1 and "Moby Dick".  Pretty hilarious, to bad you can't save replays from multiplayer.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)||||reg||10
Z||000003||loafer87gt||01-17-2001||11:23 AM||||Standard: You mentioned you are having probs with lock ups, any chance you are using a Nvidia card? I used to get lock ups using my GeForce DDR card until I downloaded the new 6.31 drivers. <P>I'm partial to the early 70's 911 turbos. I love to reinact the big Porsche chase scene from the movie Condor Man with my Black 911T. I agree, the game is too cool. The sequel to it should be out this summer. It is called Motor City, and allows you to buy any old muscle car and mod the heck out it. It is an online game, so you meet up with guys at one of the big meeting places and race for virtual cash or pink slips. I think it should be great, and the graphics are looking amazing. I'm looking forward to getting my hands on a Judge and tweaking the heck out of it!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||overlord||01-17-2001||12:23 PM||||yes motorcity is going to RULE.<BR>Ive been waiting for this game for almost a year now. Ive got nfs3, 4,5....and by far in my opinion is nfs3....me and my cousin used to play that thing every day over the modem. Me with my fiero and him with his trans-am. Damn that was fun....had some good replays of the fiero outcorning that heavy ol tranny.<BR>Damn,,,,now im gonna have to download a fiero for it and install it again.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Songman||01-17-2001||05:03 PM||||I've got an NVidia card... I may have to check out the drivers....<P>I just can't find a way to get from the garage to the race in Porsche Unleashed... Once I git something and it went to the test track... That's it! The game is not patched or anything. As a matter of fact, I just reinstalled it the other day.<P>Is there some obvious way to get from the garage to the tracks? Hints?<P>I was using Windows 2000 and went back to ME because none of my games and hardly any of my peripherals would work. Now I am thinking of going back to 2000 since they should have support for more stuff by now... and besides, ME bites! It is so dang slow!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pontiaddict||01-17-2001||05:07 PM||||I remember cheating my way through Porsche Unleashed. I used a hex edit program to make $100,000,000 and buy most of the cars and fix them up. Then I renamed the tracks that I couldn't beat in Career mode to ones I could, then beat that. Then I renamed some files to make most of my cars have the GT1 engine. *Tim Allen Grunt* <BR>That 356 coupe really moves when you do that, especially when the boost hits. Did the Autobahn in 4min 32 sec with it. It doesn't handle very well at that speed for some reason though. I usually drive the Boxster spins the tires into 4th.<P>As you can tell, I don't like to play fair, but don't worry, I usually still lose (but not against the computer because most of them have the old 356 engine or no engine at all.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>I recently deleted the game, so I can't remember the details of how I did all of that stuff. (I still have my saved game though if I ever reinstall it.)||||reg||6
Z||000007||Pontiaddict||01-17-2001||05:14 PM||||In the garage, you have to click on the bottom of the screen where it flashes race in blue. (if I remember correctly)||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||01-18-2001||12:05 AM||||In the bottom right hand of the screen, next to the options, will be a rotating yellow "Race" button.  Click that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>As for the lockup issue, I'm running on a K6-2 300, used to have it o/c'd to 350 but dropped it back down 'cause I thought that might be the problem, but it wasn't.. Diamond Monster Fusion (voodoo banshee) Won't run with the diamond drivers, and I've tried 3 different versions of the 3dfx reference drivers.  Made a different startup config with everything I didn't need disabled.. just downloaded the 3.5 patch.  <P>I think the main problem was after the first few lockups I didn't run scandisk.. when I finally ran it there was around 200 megs worth of lost file fragments, all from NFS5 I'm pretty sure.  Cleaned that up, defragged my disk,  and now I can usually play for 5 hours w/o a lockup  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  But once it does lock up it will get more and more frequent unless I run scandisk..  I just put it on our other computer to see if it will lock up on there, but so far so good.  I have heard of a few other people having the random lock-up problem, and about the problems with the Geforce..<P>Those 70's porsches are too hard to handle!  Especially the 75 and 78 turbo's!  You touch the gas in a corner and you're gone, even with slicks..  The 944 handles perfect, and with the turbo it has some pretty good speed.  Also like the 914 2.0, even though it has no power.  Reminds me of a 2m4  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I have one profile where I cheated, but it just made it too boring.. Plus, it's pretty easy to get a lot of money buying and selling the used cars.  No matter what you buy, you'll always make a profit.  I've made 100,000 selling the 935 whale tail's at the start of the modern era, and have 4 or 5 of them now 'cause their value jumps to over a million later on.<P>Motor City looks awesome, but then I'll have to get a DSL connection...||||reg||
Z||000009||Pontiaddict||01-18-2001||05:44 PM||||I didn't start cheating until the game screwed me over by corrupting my saved game file. I have the beta and it isn't complete Thats why the button was blue instead of yellow.<BR>I finally got sick of it and deleted it.<P>Oh, hold on to the first year Porsche because you can't get it anywhere at the end of the game.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Standard||01-20-2001||04:13 AM||||Hold onto all your 356's.. after about halfway through the golden era it's pretty much immpossible to get any 356 except a few 356 b's..  and buy a few extra cabriolet's, their value jumps to around the 100,000 dollar range, depending on the model..<P>Just finished the evolution mode yesterday, got all 80 cars with about 5 million in the bank  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  man the GT1 rocks!||||reg||1
